    "question": "There are 4,000 jelly beans in a jar. If three fourths of the jelly beans are red, and one quarter of the red jelly beans are coconut flavored, how many jelly beans are coconut flavored?",
    "gold": "750",
    "answer": "There are 4000/4*3=<<4000/4*3=3000>>3000 red jelly beans.\nThere are 3000/4=<<3000/4=750>>750 coconut flavored jelly beans.\n#### 750"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine the number of coconut flavored jelly beans, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the number of red jelly beans.\n2. Determine the number of coconut flavored jelly beans from the red jelly beans.\n\nFirst, we calculate the number of red jelly beans. Since three fourths of the jelly beans are red, we multiply the total number of jelly beans by \\(\\frac{3}{4}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\text{Number of red jelly beans} = 4000 \\times \\frac{3}{4} = 4000 \\times 0.75 = 3000\n\\]\n\nNext, we find out how many of these red jelly beans are coconut flavored. Since one quarter of the red jelly beans are coconut flavored, we multiply the number of red jelly beans by \\(\\frac{1}{4}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\text{Number of coconut flavored jelly beans} = 3000 \\times \\frac{1}{4} = 3000 \\times 0.25 = 750\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the number of coconut flavored jelly beans is \\(\\boxed{750}\\).",
